You are looking at the pre-V19 neon_route. Since V02 rev 2 the code is V19s exact split (no op5, no (insn & 0x60) test):

    if (bit23 == 0) return neon_3same;
    if (bit4) {
        if (((insn >> 19) & 7) == 0 && ((insn >> 7) & 1) == 0) return neon_misc;  /* one-reg modified imm */
        return neon_shift;
    }
    if (((insn >> 20) & 3) == 3) return neon_misc;  /* two-reg misc */
    return neon_shift;

Your three words under this rule: vmov.i32 d0,#0xff = f387001f (bit4=1, bits21-19=0, bit7=0) -> neon_misc; vmov.f32 d0,#1.0 = f2870f10 -> neon_misc; vorr.i32 d0,#0xff = f387011f -> neon_misc. vaddl.s8 f2810002 and vaddhn f2820404 have bit4=0 -> neon_shift (V19), as before. I added those three plus V19s five regression words to test_v02 (llvm-mc generated); the suite is N2TEST V02 PASS 842/842 (ASan+UBSan 404, -O2 404, TSan 34). So no change is needed and nothing of yours is being sent to V19.

Your 0xF4 observation matches the table: F4/F5 PLI/PLD/PLDW are caught by exact masks before neon_ldst (PLI immediate is 0xF45/0xF4D, i.e. bit20=1, which your set excludes), and everything else in F4 goes to n2a32_neon_ldst, which returns UNDEF for anything outside the structure-ld/st space. If your DONE run sees a word outside {0,2,8,A,4,6,C,E} that is a real VLDn/VSTn, send it and I will extend the mask.
